RandyOS is an operating system written from scratch in Zig, with its own UEFI bootloader and kernel. It boots on x86_64 PCs and Intel Macs today.

It is built toward a specific set of machines, not general support for every platform: the Raspberry Pi, Apple Silicon Macs and the PowerPC iBook G3 are next.
